  <span class=sf-dump-index>3</span> => <span class=sf-dump-note>array:22</span> [<samp data-depth=2 class=sf-dump-compact>
    \"<span class=sf-dump-key>id</span>\" => <span class=sf-dump-num>1523</span>
    \"<span class=sf-dump-key>name</span>\" => \"<span class=sf-dump-str title=\"152 characters\">Psychological Interventions Enhancing Social Support for Breastfeeding Mothers in Bulawayo Clinics: The Roles of Counselling and Community Psychologists</span>\"
    \"<span class=sf-dump-key>slug</span>\" => \"<span class=sf-dump-str title=\"151 characters\">Psychological-Interventions-Enhancing-Social-Support-for-Breastfeeding-Mothers-in-Bulawayo-Clinics-The-Roles-of-Counselling-and-Community-Psychologists</span>\"
    \"<span class=sf-dump-key>aname</span>\" => \"<span class=sf-dump-str title=\"34 characters\">Mpofu Brian*, Dr Siziba Khumbulani</span>\"
    \"<span class=sf-dump-key>abstract</span>\" => \"\"\"
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"3142 characters\">&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, &amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;; margin: 8px 0in 0px; text-align: justify; font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;serif&amp;quot;; color: rgb(15, 17, 21); background: white;&quot;&gt;Breastfeeding is critical for maternal<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"3142 characters\">            and child health, yet rates in Bulawayo remain suboptimal due to psychosocial<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"3142 characters\">            barriers including stress, low maternal confidence, and weak social support.<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"3142 characters\">            Current healthcare systems often neglect integrated psychological and<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"3142 characters\">            community-based interventions. This study examined psychosocial challenges<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"3142 characters\">            hindering breastfeeding practices and determined how integrated counselling and<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"3142 characters\">            community psychology interventions can strengthen social support systems in<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"3142 characters\">            Bulawayo clinics. Guided by Bronfenbrenner&#039;s Ecological Systems Theory and<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"3142 characters\">            Cohen and Wills&#039; Social Support Theory, this qualitative study adopted an<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"3142 characters\">            interpretivist philosophy and multiple case study design. Purposive sampling<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"3142 characters\">            selected 20 breastfeeding mothers, 10 healthcare providers, and 5 counselling<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"3142 characters\">            psychologists from Bulawayo clinics. Data were collected through<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"3142 characters\">            semi-structured interviews and focus group discussions, and analysed using<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"3142 characters\">            Braun and Clarke&#039;s thematic analysis framework. Two themes emerged:<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"3142 characters\">            psychosocial challenges hindering breastfeeding, with subthemes of<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"3142 characters\">            psychological distress and low self-efficacy, cultural beliefs and<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"3142 characters\">            misconceptions (particularly intergenerational transmission of colostrum<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"3142 characters\">            avoidance), and weak social support networks creating a &quot;support<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"3142 characters\">            vacuum&quot;. The second theme identified integrated interventions<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"3142 characters\">            strengthening social support, including counselling psychology interventions<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"3142 characters\">            addressing individual psychological needs, community psychology interventions<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"3142 characters\">            reducing social isolation, and integrated collaborative approaches combining both<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"3142 characters\">            strategies. Novel findings include the intergenerational transmission of<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"3142 characters\">            harmful cultural beliefs and recognition that neither counselling nor community<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"3142 characters\">            interventions alone are sufficient. Breastfeeding mothers in Bulawayo face<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"3142 characters\">            significant psychosocial challenges requiring comprehensive support. Integrated<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"3142 characters\">            counselling and community psychology interventions addressing both individual<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"3142 characters\">            and systemic factors are essential but currently unavailable. Integrate<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"3142 characters\">            counselling psychology services into routine maternal healthcare, establish<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"3142 characters\">            community-based peer support networks, implement culturally sensitive education<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
      <span class=sf-dump-str title=\"3142 characters\">            engaging elders and develop integrated intervention frameworks with adequate<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\r\\n</span></span>
