  <span class=sf-dump-index>16</span> => <span class=sf-dump-note>array:15</span> [<samp data-depth=2 class=sf-dump-compact>
    \"<span class=sf-dump-key>id</span>\" => <span class=sf-dump-num>16</span>
    \"<span class=sf-dump-key>journal_id</span>\" => <span class=sf-dump-num>1</span>
    \"<span class=sf-dump-key>parent_id</span>\" => <span class=sf-dump-num>7</span>
    \"<span class=sf-dump-key>title</span>\" => \"<span class=sf-dump-str title=\"17 characters\">Editor Guidelines</span>\"
    \"<span class=sf-dump-key>slug</span>\" => \"<span class=sf-dump-str title=\"17 characters\">editor-guidelines</span>\"
    \"<span class=sf-dump-key>type</span>\" => \"<span class=sf-dump-str title=\"7 characters\">content</span>\"
    \"<span class=sf-dump-key>system_key</span>\" => <span class=sf-dump-const>null</span>
    \"<span class=sf-dump-key>content</span>\" => \"<span class=sf-dump-str title=\"3111 characters\">&lt;p&gt;Editorial Board Members Role and Responsibilities&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The editorial board, also referred to as the (editorial) advisory committee, is comprised of experts in the journal&#039;s field, some of whom may serve on other journal boards. Their roles and responsibilities include:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. Expertise in Subject Matter:&lt;/strong&gt; Editorial board members should have a strong background and expertise in the subject matter covered by the journal.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. Reviewing Submitted Manuscripts:&lt;/strong&gt; They are responsible for reviewing and evaluating manuscripts submitted to the journal, providing constructive feedback, and making recommendations for publication.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. Advising on Journal Policy and Scope:&lt;/strong&gt; Editorial board members offer guidance on the journal&#039;s policies, focus, and scope, ensuring alignment with the field&#039;s current trends and needs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4. Identifying Special Topics and Conferences:&lt;/strong&gt; They can propose special issue topics and may assist in organizing and guest-editing these issues. This helps diversify journal content.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5. Attracting Authors:&lt;/strong&gt; Board members can actively encourage researchers to submit their work to the journal, expanding its author base.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;6. Submitting Their Work:&lt;/strong&gt; Ideally, board members should contribute their own research to the journal, setting an example for potential authors.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;7. Maintaining Manuscript Flow:&lt;/strong&gt; Ensuring a steady flow of high-quality manuscripts to the publishing house to meet the journal&#039;s publication schedule.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;8. Staying Informed:&lt;/strong&gt; Keeping abreast of changes and emerging trends in the field to reflect these shifts in the journal&#039;s content. This may involve inviting articles or special issues.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;9. Participating in Editorial Board Selection:&lt;/strong&gt; Collaborating with the publishing contact to select new editorial board members who can contribute effectively.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;10. Engaging with the Board:&lt;/strong&gt; Regularly updating and involving the editorial board in the journal&#039;s progress and development through formal or informal meetings.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;11. Providing Strategic Input:&lt;/strong&gt; Offering strategic insights for the journal&#039;s growth and development, which the publishing contact can use for guidance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;12. Promoting Revenue Opportunities:&lt;/strong&gt; Encouraging commercial advertising, supplements, and reprint options that contribute to the journal&#039;s revenue.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;13. Promoting the Journal:&lt;/strong&gt; Actively promoting the journal within their professional networks, among peers, and to colleagues, thereby increasing its visibility.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Given the large number of submissions and the journal&#039;s broad scope, one editor alone may not make informed decisions across all subject areas. Hence, editorial roles are often categorized, including Editor-in-Chief, Co-Editors, Associate Editors, Section Editors, Editorial Advisors, External Editors, and Guest Editors. Each plays a specific role in ensuring the journal&#039;s success and relevance in its field.&lt;/p&gt;<span class=\"sf-dump-default sf-dump-ns\">\\n</span></span>\"
    \"<span class=sf-dump-key>sort_order</span>\" => <span class=sf-dump-num>90</span>
    \"<span class=sf-dump-key>is_published</span>\" => <span class=sf-dump-num>1</span>
    \"<span class=sf-dump-key>show_in_nav</span>\" => <span class=sf-dump-num>1</span>
    \"<span class=sf-dump-key>show_in_tabs</span>\" => <span class=sf-dump-num>0</span>
