    \"<span class=sf-dump-key>content</span>\" => \"<span class=sf-dump-str title=\"2391 characters\">&lt;p&gt;The process for preparing a manuscript for submission to the journal is outlined as follows:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Page Format:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Manuscripts should be submitted in English or according to the journal&#039;s criteria.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Format the document as a Microsoft Word file.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Use Times New Roman font with a size of 10.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Set the page size to A4.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The text must be within 30 printable pages.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Maintain 1-inch margins on all four sides.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Use 2 column layout.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Ensure single-spaced line spacing throughout the document, including references and tables.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manuscript Structure:&lt;/strong&gt; The manuscript should be organized using the following headings:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Title of Manuscript: A concise and descriptive title.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Author Information:&lt;/strong&gt; Provide complete author information, including full names, affiliations, email addresses, and phone numbers. Designate the corresponding author.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Abstract:&lt;/strong&gt; Compose an abstract that summarizes the work within a single paragraph of no more than 300 words. Avoid subheadings and keep it concise.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Keywords:&lt;/strong&gt; Select 5 to 7 keywords that help readers understand the essential concepts in your manuscript, particularly for complex or less common terms.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Introduction:&lt;/strong&gt; Clearly articulate the current issues or context relevant to the research.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Materials and Methods:&lt;/strong&gt; Thoroughly explain the research methods used in your study to ensure clarity and reproducibility.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Results and Discussion:&lt;/strong&gt; Present research results, interpretations, speculations, and prospects for future research or developments.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Conclusion:&lt;/strong&gt; Summarize the outcomes of your work, highlight significant findings, and share your viewpoint.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Acknowledgment (Optional):&lt;/strong&gt; Include brief acknowledgments, grant details, and funding information if applicable.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;References:&lt;/strong&gt; Cite references in square brackets within the text. List references at the end of the manuscript following the APA Citation Style.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;Adhering to these guidelines will help authors prepare their manuscripts for submission to the journal effectively and efficiently, ensuring clarity, consistency, and adherence to formatting requirements.&lt;/p&gt;</span>\"
    \"<span class=sf-dump-key>sort_order</span>\" => <span class=sf-dump-num>10</span>
